      "writtenOn": "2025-09-15T17:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should do it. It\u0027ll default to SHA256_RSA4096 for everything, but that can be overridden either by setting the RSA_KEY_SIZE environment variable or by updating get_key_algorithm in the vendor includes (vendor.yubihsm.keygen.sh).\n\nI don\u0027t think we need to pull from the device vars if it\u0027s just going to be 4096-bit for everything. AVB itself supports even 8192-bit and I think 16384-bit, but that seems silly.\n\nShould I still update the legacy keymapper to use 4096-bit too? So far it\u0027s been intended to match the previous signing as much as possible.",
      "parentUuid": "71b9ae9d_b44d68ca",
